2026-09-27T10:35:17.0569725Z Description:
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0570275Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0570817Z 
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0572378Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0573906Z 
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0574071Z Update Note
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0574424Z ===========
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0574893Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0575344Z 
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0575481Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0575842Z ================
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0576073Z 
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0576347Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0576949Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0577310Z 
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0577501Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0577945Z ====================================
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0578235Z 
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0578461Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0579141Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0579738Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0580861Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0582048Z 
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0582227Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0582968Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0583867Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0584357Z 
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0584831Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0585507Z 
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0585641Z Packages
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0585954Z ========
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0586135Z 
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0588357Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0591004Z 
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0591420Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0592402Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0593709Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0594787Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0595829Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0596646Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0670342Z 
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0670600Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0671087Z ==========================
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0671578Z 
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0673594Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0675713Z 
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0676865Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0678477Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T10:35:17.0678843Z 
